    {
      "id": "027b8ee4-7bd6-4dbb-9165-ca1552ecfb3e",
      "name": "Note · 51",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1200,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## WP · 51 Approval handler (Telegram trigger): what and why\n**Input:** every tap and message in the approvals chat (and Notion approvals handed over by WP · 50). **Must be published.**\n**Rule: you always get an answer.** Tap → toast \"Got it ✔\" + the card is **closed** (edited into a one-line result, buttons removed). Reply → result or a clear note. Anything unmatched → 🤔 help note. No answer = bug.\n1. **Gate:** only Noah's chat id; anything else is ignored silently (security).\n2. **Route update:** 🌐 website answers · replies to a card (own text) · taps (A/B/C/Edit/Skip) · unmatched.\n3. **Idempotent:** acts only while the contact is *Awaiting approval*. A late/double tap closes the card as \"Already handled\", never a second email.\n4. **Legal-basis gate:** Email + Consent/Existing relationship/Inbound → **sent**. Email + *None - draft only* (all article leads) → **Gmail draft** in hello@. LinkedIn → text to paste.\n5. **Close + log:** Notion gets Status, Chosen variant, final text, timestamps, Approval log; the card is edited (✅/📝/🔗/⏭). Errors keep the card open with a ❌ reply.\n6. **One out, one in:** after a decision, WP · 50 runs at once so the next card arrives.\nDocs: docs/50-approval.md"
      }
    }
